Subject: winemac: Don't double HORZRES and VERTRES in retina mode.
Author: Alexander Theißen, athei/wine commit 6a52255e56a56e7366d5013075d2ce81149fa624 (2026-09-25, branch cx-26-patched), applied verbatim.
Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, same as Wine.
Provenance: https://github.com/athei/wine/commit/6a52255e56a56e7366d5013075d2ce81149fa624. Applied after 0001-0018 to Wine 11.19, source tarball
73eb0b02dfc0cb0ff4f4d8d36c5786261e9725ac91968ae4d4e4b9a498c4087f. Not submitted upstream by AnvilMac.
Evidence (AnvilMac, 2026-11-09, Scripts/runtime/retina-caps-check.sh on 11.19-15, M2 Pro 3456x2234): with RetinaMode=y
GetDeviceCaps HORZRES/VERTRES = 6912x4468 while DESKTOPHORZRES, SM_CXSCREEN and the display mode say 3456x2234.
AnvilMac offers RetinaMode per game (Game Settings).

From 6a52255e56a56e7366d5013075d2ce81149fa624 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Alexander=20Thei=C3=9Fen?= <alex@theissen.io>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:06:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Don't double HORZRES and VERTRES in retina mode.

macdrv_GetDeviceCaps doubled both caps whenever retina mode was on,
on top of the fallback implementation. That fallback now returns the
primary monitor rect or SM_CXSCREEN/SM_CYSCREEN, and winemac already
reports monitors in pixels in retina mode, so a retina process saw
HORZRES 6912 and VERTRES 4468 on a 3456x2234 display while
EnumDisplaySettings, GetSystemMetrics and DESKTOPHORZRES all said
3456x2234.

Team Fortress 2 centres its windowed game window from HORZRES and
VERTRES, so the window landed around the centre of a desktop twice
the real size: bottom right and partly off screen.

Pass both caps through to the fallback unchanged.
---
 dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
index 7342494a5a9..bd6ab444596 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
@@ -213,15 +213,10 @@ static INT macdrv_GetDeviceCaps(PHYSDEV dev, INT cap)
     case VERTSIZE:
         ret = vert_size;
         break;
-    case HORZRES:
-    case VERTRES:
     default:
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&device_data_mutex);
         dev = GET_NEXT_PHYSDEV( dev, pGetDeviceCaps );
-        ret = dev->funcs->pGetDeviceCaps( dev, cap );
-        if ((cap == HORZRES || cap == VERTRES) && retina_on)
-            ret *= 2;
-        return ret;
+        return dev->funcs->pGetDeviceCaps( dev, cap );
     }
 
     TRACE("cap %d -> %d\n", cap, ret);
